From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tm <tm@x>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] GC: every object relocated without overflowing the
 stack of C; a hash table is copied once

Patch 0037 bounded the recursion of relocate only through the cars of
lists: data nested deep through vectors, closures, the tails of improper
lists, gensyms or hash tables still overflowed the stack of C during a
collection, a crash. relocate now gets the depth of the object as an
argument (no global counter); past 1000 levels, any object is copied
with its fields not yet relocated (copy_object) and put on the list of
pending objects of 0037, whose fields are relocated (scan_object) before
the finalizers are swept. Without memory for that list, the recursion
goes on as before. To-space is not scanned linearly as in Cheney's
algorithm: a cons has no header which gives its type.

The keys and values of a hash table were relocated by relocate_htable
before the table was forwarded: a table which contained itself was
copied without end (a crash), and a table reachable from its values was
copied twice. relocate_htable now only makes the copy point to its own
inline space, and the collector relocates the keys and values once the
table is forwarded. The boot image does not change.
---
 flisp.c | 277 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 table.c |   8 +-
 2 files changed, 205 insertions(+), 80 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flisp.c b/flisp.c
index b6a9022ce2..c90009f0c6 100644
--- a/flisp.c
+++ b/flisp.c
@@ -428,62 +428,204 @@ void fl_free_gc_handles(uint32_t n)
     N_GCHND -= n;
